# Badge Evolution Design Rule

Before modifying any badge-related implementation, **read** `docs/design/BADGE_EVOLUTION_DESIGN_RULE.md`.

That Markdown file is the single canonical visual source of truth. The owner-approved Badge Evolution Studio geometry must be reproduced with Flutter `CustomPainter` vector primitives.

## Required

- Reuse the shared prestige frame + seven center artworks (42 combinations).
- Preserve exact palette, gradients, radii, ornament counts, stroke widths, capsule and label placement.
- Keep localization out of painters and domain math.
- Extend golden tests when geometry or catalogue changes.

## Forbidden without explicit owner approval

- Redesigning, simplifying, or replacing badge artwork
- Material Icons, emoji, AI-generated PNG medals, or generic achievement icons as substitutes
- Cap earned counts at Mythic
- Granting competitive advantages or purchasable prestige
- Resetting existing badge progress or renaming incompatible persisted IDs (especially `on_time`)
